Export exactly this API:

`func MergeUnique(left, right []int) []int`

Both inputs are sorted in nondecreasing order. Merge them into one increasing slice containing each encountered value exactly once. Duplicate values may occur within either input and across both inputs. Preserve numeric order and do not modify either input.

Return a complete source file using package `solution`. Use only the standard library. Do not access the filesystem, network, clock, or randomness.

```go
package solution

func MergeUnique(left, right []int) []int {
	merged := make([]int, 0, len(left)+len(right))
	i, j := 0, 0

	for i < len(left) && j < len(right) {
		if left[i] <= right[j] {
			merged = append(merged, left[i])
			i++
		} else {
			merged = append(merged, right[j])
			j++
		}
	}

	merged = append(merged, left[i:]...)
	merged = append(merged, right[j:]...)
	return merged
}
