Provide exactly this public API:

```go
type RevisionStore struct { /* unexported fields */ }
func NewRevisionStore(initial []string) *RevisionStore
func (s *RevisionStore) Commit(expectedVersion uint64, next []string) bool
func (s *RevisionStore) Undo() bool
func (s *RevisionStore) Snapshot() (uint64, []string)
```

A new store starts at version 0 with `initial` as its current sequence. `Commit` succeeds only when `expectedVersion` equals the current version. On success, it saves the current sequence for one-step-at-a-time undo, installs `next`, increments the version, and returns true. On a version mismatch it returns false without changing any state. Each successful `Undo` restores the most recently saved sequence, removes that history entry, increments the version, and returns true. With no saved revision, `Undo` returns false without changing the version. A commit after an undo adds a new history entry from the restored state.

The store must own all of its data: later mutation of `initial` or `next` must not affect it, and mutation of the slice returned by `Snapshot` must not affect later snapshots. Nil and empty slices may both be represented as empty snapshots; no distinction between them is required.

Return one complete source file using package `solution`. Use only the standard library. Do not access the filesystem, network, clock, or randomness.","reference_code":"package solution

type RevisionStore struct {
	version uint64
	current []string
	history [][]string
}

func NewRevisionStore(initial []string) *RevisionStore {
	return &RevisionStore{current: cloneStrings(initial)}
}

func (s *RevisionStore) Commit(expectedVersion uint64, next []string) bool {
	if expectedVersion != s.version {
		return false
	}
	s.history = append(s.history, s.current)
	s.current = cloneStrings(next)
	s.version++
	return true
}

func (s *RevisionStore) Undo() bool {
	if len(s.history) == 0 {
		return false
	}
	last := len(s.history) - 1
	s.current = s.history[last]
	s.history = s.history[:last]
	s.version++
	return true
}

func (s *RevisionStore) Snapshot() (uint64, []string) {
	return s.version, cloneStrings(s.current)
}

func cloneStrings(values []string) []string {
	if len(values) == 0 {
		return nil
	}
	copyOfValues := make([]string, len(values))
	copy(copyOfValues, values)
	return copyOfValues
}
